# Yan is new to this

Yan has no idea how Particle, Zephyr, SWD, OpenOCD, breadboards, or this repo work. Assume zero background.

Do the commands, flashing, and debugging yourself. Do not tell him to run a terminal incantation. If something needs a cable, a plug, or a glance at an LED, say that in one short sentence. If USB does not show the Particle Debugger, stop and say so. Do not pretend a flash worked.

Explain what you did and what to look at on the desk. No jargon without a translation.

Hardware as of 2026-09-15:

- Mac Studio (M3 Ultra). Two USB-A ports on the back. Debugger USB-A in one, Argon white kit USB in the other. No dongle. Front USB-C plus a dongle does not enumerate the debugger.
- Debugger: ARM DAPLink CMSIS-DAP (USB vid 0x0d28 pid 0x0204). Gray kit ribbon to the Argon 10-pin header.
- Particle Argon on a breadboard. It may not show up as a USB device. SWD through the debugger is the path that works.
- Kit bag: one round-top red LED (this is the lamp) and one flat-top phototransistor (light sensor, Everlight ALS-PT243-3C/L177). The flat one will never light. Also two 220 ohm resistors. Use a resistor in series with the round LED.
- Breadboard lamp: round LED, long leg in the D5 row, short leg in the blue strip. The two blue strips (one on each long side) are not connected to each other. Jumper an Argon GND pin to the same blue strip as the LED, even if that wire crosses the board. Active-high, nRF P1.10.
